# Input graph for MDD4REST__mdd4rest-annotator__server_src_rdflib2_plugins_sparql_results_rdfresults.py__RDFResult___init__
# — written during translation. This is the SELECT-shaped scenario (the
# region's SPARQL-results-as-RDF vocabulary, W3C result-set#): the driver
# builds two more (ASK true/false, CONSTRUCT/no-ResultSet) inline, since a
# single graph can hold only one rdf:type rs:ResultSet subject without
# making graph.value(predicate=, object=)'s "first match" pick ambiguous.
#
# Covers: several solutions of every joined pattern (two resultVariable
# entries; two solutions; sol1 has two bindings, sol2 has one); the
# zero-solution case for the inner binding join (sol3 has NO rs:binding at
# all -- the outer solution loop must still emit an empty row for it, which
# is exactly why the outer loop over solutions stays its own m{ } instead of
# being fused into the inner join: fusing solution+binding would silently
# drop sol3); and neighbourhood that must not match (ex:orphanBinding has
# the same rs:variable/rs:value shape as a real binding but is not linked
# from any solution via rs:binding; ex:notAResultSet carries a
# resultVariable-like predicate but is never typed rs:ResultSet).
@prefix rs:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/sw/DataAccess/tests/result-set#> .
@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix ex:  <http://example.org/> .

ex:rs1 a rs:ResultSet ;
    rs:resultVariable "x", "y" ;
    rs:solution ex:sol1, ex:sol2, ex:sol3, ex:sol4 .

ex:sol1 rs:binding ex:b1x, ex:b1y .
ex:b1x rs:variable "x" ; rs:value ex:alice .
ex:b1y rs:variable "y" ; rs:value "42"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .

ex:sol2 rs:binding ex:b2x .
ex:b2x rs:variable "x" ; rs:value ex:bob .
# sol2 leaves y unbound (no binding node for it in this row).

# sol3 has no rs:binding triples at all: the zero-solution case for the
# inner join, on a solution that must still produce an (empty) row.

# neighbourhood: shaped like a binding, reachable from nothing.
ex:orphanBinding rs:variable "z" ; rs:value 999 .

# neighbourhood: has a resultVariable-shaped triple but is never typed
# rs:ResultSet, so it must never be the `rs` the region binds.
ex:notAResultSet rs:resultVariable "bogus" .

# Repair of 2026-10-30 (triage: equivalence-doubt, weak-oracle).
# sol4: a binding that names its variable but carries NO rs:value -- the
# zero-solution case of the innermost value read. The region's
# `graph.value(b, RS.value)` gives None, so the row must read {x: None}; a
# translation that joins ?b rs:variable ?var . ?b rs:value ?val drops the
# binding and yields {} instead.
ex:sol4 rs:binding ex:b4x .
ex:b4x rs:variable "x" .

# Neighbours sharing two of the three terms of a region pattern, so that
# widening one bound term into a variable changes the result:
# - a non-ResultSet subject with its own rs:solution (`{rs} rs:solution ?s`
#   widened to `?x rs:solution ?s`), whose solution reaches a binding;
ex:notAResultSet rs:solution ex:straySolution .
# - a solution not reachable from ex:rs1 that links the orphan binding
#   (`{s} rs:binding ?b` widened to `?x rs:binding ?b`);
ex:straySolution rs:binding ex:orphanBinding .
# - a subject typed with something else, and one pointing at rs:ResultSet
#   through another predicate (`?rs rdf:type rs:ResultSet` widened in its
#   object or its predicate).
ex:notAResultSet rdf:type ex:SomethingElse .
ex:mentionsType ex:about rs:ResultSet .
